{"term":"apathetic","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:1f17fa18c77d880951","definition":"Void of feeling; not susceptible of deep emotion.","example":"He then added a few general offers of service, but offered as if he would be glad if they were accepted; and when Guido knelt for his parting benediction, it was given with a warmth and sincerity not often used by the apathetic and haughty minister.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["indifferent","unconcerned"],"antonyms":["furious","effusive","emotional","enthusiastic","excited","overwrought","passionate"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["apathetically","apatheticness","nonapathetic","unapathetic"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apathetic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:995958a1030a67de50","definition":"Of, or pertaining to apatheism.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":["adiaphroistic","apathetic","apathistical","blasé","blithe","deaf","cool","shiftless","dispassionate","dull","enervated","gallionic","halfhearted","heartless","impassive","ineffervescible","insouciant","indifferent","insensible","jaded","languid","languorous","Laodicean","lethargic","listless","lackadaisical","lotophagous","lukewarm","meh","mopey","nonchalant","nonplussed","otiose","phlegmatic","pococurante","spiritless","supine","tepid","torpid","torpedinous","unaroused","uncaring","unconcerned","unenthusiastic","unimpressible","uninterested","unlively","unmoved","untouched","unzealous","world-weary"],"antonyms":["furious","effusive","emotional","enthusiastic","excited","overwrought","passionate"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["apathetically","apatheticness","nonapathetic","unapathetic"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apathetic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:426e33d9e9cb58084e","definition":"An apathetic or indifferent person, especially one who shows no interest in a particular issue.","example":"On the left are the activist Vietniks, eager to protest the war; next are the doves, who oppose the U.S. role but shun demonstrations; and in the middle are the apathetics, who simply are not concerned enough to think through their own stand.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["apathetically","apatheticness","nonapathetic","unapathetic"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apathetic#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˌæpəˈθɛtɪk/"},"wordFamily":["apathetically","apatheticness","nonapathetic","unapathetic"]}